 "randomTheme": {
  "rule": "for each paintable slot, pick a material of the piece's tier allowed in that slot and on this floor, weighted by the slot's type weights below; the second plate repeats the plate's paint at the given share, so most suits are one harness rather than a patchwork of metals; then roll colour 2 on the tier's bell curve (a neutral by the neutral share, otherwise an open hue with saturation from a half-bell of the tier's width, capped at its ceiling) and colour 1 as a neutral; a metal takes no dye: its rolled colour goes on as a coat over the metal (metalCoat) when the coat roll says painted, otherwise the metal stays bare; within metal, coloured metals take colouredMetalShareByTier of the metal weight, so every grade shows its own coloured metals; a paint takes a colour finish (a fade or per pale, or on bare metal a fade into another metal) at finishShareByTier (every paint since ruling 17), and then the gradient rule keeps one fade a piece on its largest dyed surface in the part's palette family, light end up; at the grimeFades tiers (Janky) only a grime, soot or rust fade, never a clean dye fade or a per-pale split",
